# Commit messages

Short. Imperative. About the code change only.

## Format

- Subject: ≤72 chars, imperative, no trailing period
- Body: only if the why is not obvious; keep it to a few lines
- One concern per commit

```
# GOOD
Add Postgres run-state migrations

# GOOD
Fail closed when verification disagrees with the sandbox

# BAD
Fleet task github-tools: worker added PR creation on attempt 2

# BAD
Claude fixed the sandbox verification and added co-authors
```

## Never include

- Mentions of Claude, Cursor, Copilot, AI, LLMs, agents, or model names
- Fleet, workers, batches, waves, task IDs, or role names
- Any trailer: `Co-authored-by`, `Generated with`, `Signed-off-by` (unless a human explicitly asked), `Made-with`, etc.
- Attempt counts, “automated”, or process narration

`includeCoAuthoredBy` stays false. Do not add attribution in the message or via
git config. If the environment appends a trailer anyway, strip it before push —
never leave `Co-authored-by: Cursor` or `Made-with: Cursor` on `main`.

Also keep Cursor Settings → Git & PRs → Attribution (commit + PR) off.
